posts.body:
I think something like this will do what you want:
JavaScript:
Window_ItemCategory.prototype.windowHeight = function() {
    return this.fittingHeight(2);
};
Just put it in a plugin file and load it via the plugin manager.
That definitely works in MV. I'm not 100% sure if it works in MZ too, but I think it should.

By "didn't work" you mean the window is still 1 line high, right?
Hmm. I poked around a bit more, and I think this might work instead. You can open the plugin you just made in TextEdit and replace its entire content with the below code:
JavaScript:
Window_ItemCategory.prototype.maxRows = function() {
    return 2;
};
If that still fails, the problem most likely lies in VisuStella replacing base windows with their own custom windows. You could poke around in the ItemsEquipCore or MainMenuCore plugin settings to see if there's anything about this. Failing that, I do have another possible solution where you'd temporarily install a plugin to help figure out what needs to change.
